  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user who typed a moderation reason or a poll (a question and up to ten answers), I want a confirmation before a swipe-down or « Annuler » throws it away, as the main composer already does, so that I do not lose it by accident.\n\n### Rule\n\n- \"Support swiping to dismiss a sheet. […] If people have unsaved changes in the sheet when they begin swiping to dismiss it, use an action sheet to let them confirm their action.\" — [HIG › Sheets](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/sheets) (iOS, iPadOS; page updated 2026-03-24).\n- \"When necessary, help people avoid data loss by getting confirmation before closing a modal view.\" — [HIG › Modality](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/modality).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/Actions/ModeratorAlertComposerView.swift:42` `Button(\"Annuler\") { dismiss() }` and `:49` `.interactiveDismissDisabled(model.isSending)` (only while sending); the reason lives in the model, dropped when the sheet closes (`ReaderAlertFlow.swift:18`).\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Composer/PollCreationSheet.swift:68-79`: `Button(\"Annuler\") { dismiss() }`, no `interactiveDismissDisabled`; the state reaches the composer only through `onSave`.\n- The main composer handles it (`Composer/ReplyComposerView.swift:110-116`, `dismissDisabled: model.closeNeedsChoice`).\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\nSame gap: `HFRswift/Swift/MessagesView.swift:7478-7484` (plain `dismiss()`, no dismiss guard), `HFRswift/Swift/TopicPollDraft.swift:124-127`.\n\n### Class\n\n**(b) evolution, M5** (same as legacy).\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- `.interactiveDismissDisabled(hasChanges)` and a `confirmationDialog` (« Abandonner », destructive; « Continuer la saisie », cancel) on a swipe attempt and on « Annuler » when the fields differ from their initial values.\n- Check: a view-model test of the \"has unsaved text\" predicate for both sheets.\n\nRelated: #429 (the main composer's swipe-down, UXD-15).\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
