   "body": "/claim cloud/m4q-reliab-opus\n\nRe-checked on `dev-swift` @ 1b6f98f0: the problem still holds. `ModeratorAlertComposerView` « Annuler » calls `dismiss()` directly and only blocks the swipe while a send runs. `PollCreationSheet` « Annuler » calls `dismiss()` and has no swipe guard.\n\nOverlap: #1261 changes another hunk of `ReaderAlertFlow.swift` (« Oui/Non » → verbs, `AlertVerbs`); I don't need to touch that file. No other open PR touches these two sheets.\n\nPlan (same behaviour as the main composer, #429/UXD-15):\n- While there are unsaved changes, the swipe-down is blocked (`interactiveDismissDisabled`). « Annuler » then asks « Abandonner » (destructive) / « Continuer la saisie » (cancel). With nothing typed, « Annuler » closes at once as today.\n- Predicates, tested first (red today, since they do not exist):\n  - moderator alert: a non-blank reason, while the sheet has not ended;\n  - poll: the fields differ from the draft the sheet opened on.\n- One shared modifier for the dialog.\n- Ledger: a changelog row (UX). Legacy (`MessagesView.swift:7478-7484`, `TopicPollDraft.swift:124-127` @ `87fe0d1c`) closes without asking.\n- Draft PR with `compile-check`, then a Fable review.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
